njected advance fails; clear quarantine variables for the separate local object store. Also cover initial and repeated attach, migration from both legacy mappings, remote rewind and sibling refusal, concurrent append during import, custom source-branch mappings, and failed operations preserving prior local state. Use meaningful controls, not sleep-based luck or only tests of generated refspec strings.\n\nUpdate the attach reference, publish-and-audit guide and cloned-repository examples so their supported commands preserve the invariant. Keep recovery evidence separate from source delivery: immutable sibling events and saved witnesses remain preserved, and no test fixture touches a live workroom. Report one exact candidate, complete path manifest and actual test evidence, then obtain independent review and finish delivery/push/cleanup.\n\nEvidence: /tmp/planner-push-tracking-control-20260906.json; /tmp/planner-safe-push-tracking-control-20260906.json; /tmp/gitseq-frontier-fork-20260906.json; /tmp/notes-sequence-recovery-plan.md. Source locations read: cmd/gs/main.go fetchSequenceRefs and sequenceFetchRefspec; docs/reference/gs/attach.md; docs/how-to/publish-and-audit.md; docs/how-to/use-in-a-cloned-repo.md.","priority":"After recovery/Notes required cleanup and live reader update19190; before the cancellation-oracle follow-up and Tailapp recovery preparation. Coordinate with existing commitments. This is permanent prevention of the recovered incident19194, not another operational ref recovery.","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}